## Phase 4: Vision Hallucination War (26 Mar 2026 — This Session)

This was the major overhaul session where we battled AI hallucinations across 8+ iterations.

### Iteration 1 — Anti-Hallucination Rules
- Added explicit "DO NOT GUESS" rules to `INVOICE_IMAGE_PROMPT`
- Instructed AI to use `null` instead of inventing batch numbers like `AC-N007`
- **Result:** Row 1 (Naturally Churna) became 100% accurate ✅

### Iteration 2 — Top-to-Bottom Scanning
- Fixed the "reverse jump" bug where AI read from bottom to top
- Added serial number anchoring (1, 2, 3... in order)
- **Result:** Rows extracted in correct order ✅

### Iteration 3 — Sr.No JSON Anchoring
- Added `srNo` field to the JSON output as a positional anchor
- Instructed AI to look "straight down" from column headers
- **Result:** Batch numbers for Row 1 now correct (CH0087) ✅

### Iteration 4 — Duplicate Medicine Merging ([dedup()](file:///C:/Users/vaibh/Documents/Ayur-stock%20pro/lib/aiParser.ts#196-234))
- Created [dedup()](file:///C:/Users/vaibh/Documents/Ayur-stock%20pro/lib/aiParser.ts#196-234) function that merges rows with same name + company + packing
- Sums quantities: Row 1 (72) + Row 2 (48) = **120**
- Keeps best available data from each row
- **Result:** Two "Naturally Churna" rows merged into one ✅

### Iteration 5 — Quality-Based Model Fallback
- Added quality checker: if >40% of rows have missing batch/qty → reject and try next tier
- Forces fallback to Gemini 2.0 Flash or Claude 3.5 Sonnet for better accuracy
- **Result:** System now auto-recovers from poor Groq extractions ✅

### Iteration 6 — Model Tier Upgrades
- **Groq:** Prioritized `llama-3.3-70b-versatile` over smaller 17B model
- **OpenRouter:** Added `gemini-2.0-flash-001`, `gemini-2.0-flash-lite-001`, `claude-3.5-sonnet:beta`
- Removed low-quality free models (`nvidia-nemotron-nano-12b`, `gemma-3-4b`)

### Iteration 7 — Packing Normalization ([normalizePacking()](file:///C:/Users/vaibh/Documents/Ayur-stock%20pro/lib/aiParser.ts#593-623))
- Created function to standardize AI output to UI dropdown values
- `100GM` → `100 gm`, `30TAB` → `30 Tab`, `200ML` → `200 ml`

### Iteration 8 — Full-Screen Review UI Redesign
- Expanded modal from `max-w-6xl` to **`98vw`** (nearly full screen)
- Increased all font sizes from `text-xs` to `text-sm`
- Bolded MRP/PTS/Qty values for quick visual scanning
- Added dedicated "Review & Validate Bill" header with inline Import button
- Hidden step indicator during review to maximize table space

### Iteration 9 — Expiry Date Normalization ([normalizeExpiryDate()](file:///c:/Users/vaibh/Documents/Ayur-stock%20pro/lib/aiParser.ts#624-670))
- Converts `Sep-26` → `2026-09-30` (last day of month, pharmacy standard)
- Handles formats: `MMM-YY`, `MMM-YYYY`, `MM/YY`, `MM-YY`

### Iteration 10 — PTR/PTS/CD% Price Distinction
- **PTS** → `purchaseRate` (what you paid)
- **PTR** → `tradePrice` (retailer reference)
- **MRP** → `mrp` (maximum retail)
- **Disc%** → `discount` (trade discount)
- **CD%** → `cashDiscount` (cash discount)

### Iteration 11 — Invoice Metadata Extraction
- AI now extracts from the invoice header:
  - `invoiceNumber` (e.g. `AIU25G6408`)
  - `invoiceDate` (e.g. `27-Feb-26`)
  - `supplierName` (e.g. `AYUKALP UAP PHARMA PVT LTD`)
- Updated [parseJsonSafely()](file:///C:/Users/vaibh/Documents/Ayur-stock%20pro/lib/aiParser.ts#235-284) to handle `{medicines: [...]}` object format

### Iteration 12 — Generalized Prompt
- Removed all Ayukalp-specific hardcoding (specific row hints, medicine names)
- Prompt now works with ANY Indian pharmacy invoice by reading column headers dynamically

